# A drag over cells, which is what a single click and a pull across the screen
# comes to. Both ends travel on every call: the anchor is the app's to keep,
# and nothing here is a range the app computed.
out "hello world\x0d\x0agoodbye"
select 0 0 4 0 cell
# Pulled on to the second row, so the golden holds a selection over two rows
# and not only a run inside one.
select 0 0 3 1 cell
copy
# The same two corners as a block, which takes the columns and not the run of
# text between them. ⌥ is what asks for it.
select 0 0 3 1 cell rectangle
copy
# And a drag once the child has asked to hear about the mouse, which selects
# nothing at all: that drag is the program's. The block above is still what
# the screen shows, and the wake count is what says no frame went out for the
# gesture that was kept.
out "\x1b[?1000h"
select 0 0 8 0 cell
select 0 0 8 1 cell
copy
